<title>UK: Minerva sets small premium on debut.</title>
<headline>Minerva sets small premium on debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Minerva Plc set a slight premium on their first day of trading on London Stock Exchange on Thursday.</p>
<p>By 1055 GMT the shares were quoted at 151p in light trade of 70,591 shares. They were placed at 150p in an issue valuing the property company at 144.0 million stg and raising 70.6 million stg.</p>
<p>The proceeds of the float, sponsored by HSBC Samuel Montagu, will be used to expand and develop Minerva's property portfolio and to finance the acquisition of a property in Wigmore Street, in the west end of London, which was conditional on the float.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
